---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy" description="How Coding Shuffle Duel handles your data." showBack={true}>
  <div class="page-header">
    <div class="hero-badge">
      <img src="/icons/locked_icon.png" alt="" class="badge-icon" />
      Legal
    </div>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="meta">Effective date: July 1, 2026 · Coding Shuffle Duel</p>
  </div>

  <div class="content-card">
    <p>
      Coding Shuffle Duel is built on a simple principle: <strong style="color: var(--text)">your data belongs to you</strong>.
      The game is designed to run entirely on your device, with no account required and no data ever
      leaving your phone unless you explicitly choose otherwise.
    </p>

    <hr class="divider" />

    <h2>1. Our Core Architecture: Offline-First</h2>
    <p>
      Coding Shuffle Duel is a fully offline application. All gameplay, progress, XP, stars, and
      achievements are stored locally on your device by default. No internet connection is required
      to play, and no data is transmitted to any server unless you create an optional account.
    </p>
    <p>
      This means the vast majority of players will never have any personal data collected, stored,
      or processed by us — full stop.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Optional Accounts & Cloud Sync</h2>
    <p>
      If you choose to create an account to sync your progress across devices, we collect only the
      minimum information necessary:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Email address</strong> — used solely for account authentication and recovery.</li>
      <li><strong>Username</strong> — a display name of your choosing (does not need to be your real name).</li>
      <li><strong>Game progress</strong> — XP earned, levels completed, and in-game achievements.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      That is the complete list. We collect nothing else. No device identifiers, no location data,
      no usage analytics, no crash reports, no behavioral tracking — nothing beyond what is listed above.
    </p>

    <h2>3. What We Do Not Collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Real name or any personally identifying information beyond email</li>
      <li>Location or IP address logs</li>
      <li>Device model, OS version, or hardware identifiers</li>
      <li>Browsing or app usage behavior</li>
      <li>Payment or financial information (the app is free)</li>
      <li>Any data from users who play without an account</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. Data Security</h2>
    <p>
      Account passwords are never stored in plain text — they are hashed using industry-standard
      cryptographic methods before storage. Your account data is hosted on a reputable cloud
      infrastructure provider with encryption in transit (TLS) and at rest.
    </p>
    <p>
      Access to the database is strictly limited and no team member has routine access to individual
      user records.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Data Sharing & Third Parties</h2>
    <p>
      We do not share, sell, rent, trade, or otherwise disclose your data to any third party, ever.
      There are no advertising networks, analytics providers, data brokers, or any other external
      services that receive your information.
    </p>
    <p>
      The only third-party involvement is our cloud hosting and database provider, who processes
      your data solely to store it on our behalf and is contractually prohibited from using it for
      any other purpose.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Voluntary Support & Ads</h2>
    <p>
      Coding Shuffle Duel is completely free and contains no forced advertisements. We offer an
      optional "Support Us" section where you can choose to watch ads voluntarily as a way to
      support the development of the game — similar to a donation. This is entirely opt-in.
      No data is collected as part of this interaction beyond what our hosting provider already logs.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Your Data Rights</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Access</strong> — Your progress and account data are always visible to you directly within the app.</li>
      <li><strong>Deletion (no account)</strong> — Uninstalling the app or clearing app data from your device settings permanently and irreversibly deletes all local data.</li>
      <li><strong>Deletion (with account)</strong> — You can delete your account and all associated data at any time from the Settings page inside the app. Deletion is immediate and permanent.</li>
      <li><strong>Portability</strong> — Your in-game progress is yours. We do not lock you in.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>8. A Note on Global Compliance</h2>
    <p>
      Because Coding Shuffle Duel is offline-first and collects no data from players without
      accounts, there are no international data transfers, cross-border processing concerns, or
      jurisdictional complications for the overwhelming majority of users.
    </p>
    <p>
      For the small subset of users who create accounts, data is stored securely on our cloud
      provider and is subject to the same protections regardless of where you are in the world.
      Coding Shuffle Duel works the same way for every player, everywhere.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Children's Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      We do not knowingly collect any personal information from children under the age of 13.
      Since no account is required to play, children can enjoy the full game experience
      without providing any data whatsoever.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>
      If we make material changes to this policy, we will update the effective date above and,
      where possible, notify users with accounts via the app or email. Continued use of the app
      after any update constitutes acceptance of the revised policy.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Contact Us</h2>
    <p>
      Questions or concerns about this Privacy Policy? We're happy to talk.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="mailto:codingshuffleduel@gmail.com">codingshuffleduel@gmail.com</a>
    </p>

    <hr class="divider" />

    <h2>Your Consent</h2>
    <p>By using Coding Shuffle Duel, you acknowledge that:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>You understand the game runs entirely offline by default, with no data collected.</li>
      <li>Account creation is optional and only you can initiate it.</li>
      <li>If you create an account, only your email, username, and game progress are stored.</li>
      <li>We do not share your data with anyone, for any reason.</li>
      <li>You are in full control of your data and can delete it at any time.</li>
      <li>Uninstalling the app without an account permanently deletes all local data.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .badge-icon {
    width: 18px;
    height: 18px;
    object-fit: contain;
    vertical-align: middle;
  }
</style>